Implementation complete. Here's the summary.

## What changed

**`tools/ai-autonomy.php` — D1 (trust surface contract-unreachable)**
- Added `trustSurfacePaths()` (the seven enumerated files) and `isTrustSurfacePath()` (fail-closed: exact file, covering directory, glob that could match, unresolved/trust-resolving symlink).
- Added one `absolute` entry to the existing single `l4Taxonomy()` list (`matchers => ['trust_surface']`), with a comment recording the 2026-09-14 owner directive, constituting-change status, and director-only amendments.
- `plan` refuses (exit 2) a contract naming a trust-surface file/glob in allowed/baseline scope. A broad `tools/` directory is not refused at plan time.
- `check` applies the matcher to `--path` **and** to path-shaped action tokens, so it escalates even when the path is inside `allowed_scope`.

**`tools/ai-run.php` — D2 + D3**
- `start` records `trust_surface_hash` (sha256 of the seven files, sorted, concatenated) plus per-file digests.
- `commit-check` recomputes and blocks (`NOT ELIGIBLE`, exit 3) on mismatch, naming moved files; legacy records without a hash are not blocked (documented trade-off).
- Malformed/unreadable run records are now blocking (`unreadable`, exit 3, naming the file) instead of being silently dropped.

**`tools/ai-project.php` — D4**
- `assertRunReDerived()` now binds `record['id'] === $runId`, start-time contract revision vs the slice contract's current revision, `claim_verification.contract_revision`, recorded `rev === git rev-parse HEAD`, and `dirty === false`. `verify` now carries the contract revision into the evidence record.

**Tests**: added 40/40a/41–45 (`ai_autonomy`), 3a/25a–25c (`ai_run`), 12–16 (`ai_project`), plus a `trust_surface` probe in the taxonomy loop.

